# A DHCPREQUEST in the SELECTING state as a relay agent forwards it, reconstructed by
# hand: hops 1, giaddr 192.0.2.1, requested address and server identifier, the client FQDN
# (RFC 4702, flags S and E, canonical wire encoding) and option 82 with circuit ID and
# remote ID (RFC 3046). Documentation addresses (RFC 5737).
#
# op 1, htype 1, hlen 6, hops 1
01 01 06 01
# xid
1c 0f fe e1
# secs, flags
00 04 00 00
# ciaddr 0.0.0.0
00 00 00 00
# yiaddr 0.0.0.0
00 00 00 00
# siaddr 0.0.0.0
00 00 00 00
# giaddr 192.0.2.1
c0 00 02 01
# chaddr
00 00 5e 00 53 03 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
# sname: empty
00*64
# file: empty
00*128
# magic cookie
63 82 53 63
# option 53: DHCPREQUEST
35 01 03
# option 61: client identifier, type 1 and the MAC
3d 07 01 00 00 5e 00 53 03
# option 50: requested address 192.0.2.50
32 04 c0 00 02 32
# option 54: server identifier 198.51.100.10
36 04 c6 33 64 0a
# option 12: host name "host-01"
0c 07 68 6f 73 74 2d 30 31
# option 81: client FQDN: flags S and E, RCODEs 0, host-01.example.test.
51 19 05 00 00 07 68 6f 73 74 2d 30 31 07 65 78
61 6d 70 6c 65 04 74 65 73 74 00
# option 55: parameter request list
37 05 01 03 06 0f 77
# option 82: relay agent information: circuit ID 0004000a0003, remote ID the relay MAC
52 10 01 06 00 04 00 0a 00 03 02 06 00 00 5e 00
53 fe
# end
ff
